esina is a versatile medication that addresses both the symptoms of diabetes insipidus and the complications associated with sodium imbalances.\",4\r\n3753,DIABETES INSÍPIDA,\"Diabetes insípida is a medical condition characterized by excessive thirst (polydipsia) and the excretion of large amounts of severely diluted urine (polyuria), leading to an imbalance in body fluids. This disorder arises from the body's inability to concentrate urine, often due to dysfunctions in the hypothalamus or pituitary gland. It can be associated with neurogenic causes, such as necrosis of the neurohypophysis, and may also occur as a result of untreated adrenal insufficiency. In some cases, it is linked to the presence of pituitary adenomas or hypothalamic damage due to pineal tumors, which disrupt the regulation of water in the body. The condition is discussed in the context of treatment options, including glucocorticoid replacement therapy, as outlined in the Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición.\",17\r\n6186,RADIOTERAPIA HIPOFISARIA,\"RADIOTERAPIA HIPOFISARIA, or hypophyseal radiotherapy, is a specialized treatment method designed to target pituitary adenomas while minimizing radiation exposure to the surrounding brain structures. This approach is particularly effective in treating these types of tumors without causing adverse effects such as hyponatremia or diabetes insipidus.\",2\r\n4025,AMILORIDA,Amilorida is a medication mentioned in the treatment of nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.,1\r\n4013,MUERTE CEREBRAL,\"Muerte cerebral refers to a state of irreversible loss of all brain functions, often leading to complications such as diabetes insípida neurogénica.\",1\r\n4019,IONES,Iones refer to charged particles that are monitored in patients with diabetes insípida and SIADH to manage electrolyte balance.,1\r\n4024,TÍA,\"Tía refers to thiazide diuretics, which are mentioned as part of the treatment for nephrogenic diabetes insipidus.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_i